{"ClientSettings":{"Pn":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"P"},"Sc":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"H"},"Qz":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"T"},"Ap":true,"Mute":true,"Lad":"2026-10-20T00:00:00Z","Iotd":0,"Gwb":0,"Tns":0,"Dft":null,"Mvs":0,"Flt":0,"Imp":1,"Tobn":0},"MediaContents":[{"ImageContent":{"Description":"What if a city's busiest street had no road? In Venice, Italy, traffic flows along the Grand Canal, a 3.8-kilometre waterway that winds through the city in a giant reverse S-shape. Known to locals as the Canalazzo, it is Venice's main water-traffic corridor, carrying vaporetti, water taxis, gondolas, police boats and other vessels. The canal follows the course of an ancient river that once flowed into the Venetian Lagoon.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.VeniceSunrise_EN-CA8133659672_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.VeniceSunrise_EN-CA8133659672_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"The road that runs on water","Title":"Grand Canal in Venice, Italy","Copyright":"© Juan Romero/Cavan Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/45.435337,12.32783/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-CA&od=2&shading=flat&pp=45.435337,12.32783;S9;Grand Canal, Venice, Italy&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261019_VeniceSunrise\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Grand+Canal+Venice&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261019_0400\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261019_VeniceSunrise"},"Ssd":"20261019","Name":"VeniceSunrise","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"8133659672","FullDateString":"Oct 19, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"If parks could keep birthday diaries, Eryri National Park (Snowdonia) in Wales would have quite the story to tell. The park turns 75 today, marking the anniversary of its designation in 1951. Eryri stretches across 2,130 square kilometres, with nine mountain ranges, 119 kilometres of coastline and habitats ranging from peatlands and native woodlands to upland landscapes. At more than 1,050 metres, Yr Wyddfa is Eryri's highest point. Nearby, the Carneddau and Glyderau add their own peaks, while Cadair Idris rises in the south. These protected landscapes provide habitats for wildlife and include 17 National Nature Reserves and 56 Sites of Special Scientific Interest.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.DolbadarnWales_EN-CA7756366430_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.DolbadarnWales_EN-CA7756366430_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"75 and thriving","Title":"Dolbadarn Castle, Llanberis, Eryri National Park (Snowdonia), Wales","Copyright":"© joe daniel price/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/52.927253,-4.077652/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-CA&od=2&shading=flat&pp=52.927253,-4.077652;S9;Eryri National Park, Wales&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261018_DolbadarnWales\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Eryri+National+Park+Wales&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261018_0400\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261018_DolbadarnWales"},"Ssd":"20261018","Name":"DolbadarnWales","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"7756366430","FullDateString":"Oct 18, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Some discoveries start with a shovel. Others start with a drawing on a cave wall. International Archaeology Day celebrates both the detective work and the evidence behind them. Organised by the Archaeological Institute of America, this annual event began in 2011 and became International Archaeology Day in 2013 as participation expanded worldwide. Today, it brings archaeology closer to the public through talks, museum programmes, site visits, simulated digs and hands-on activities.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.ChauvetPaintingsFrance_EN-CA7438357428_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.ChauvetPaintingsFrance_EN-CA7438357428_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":false},"Headline":"The past, unearthed","Title":"Life-size replica of Chauvet Cave art in Vallon-Pont-d'Arc, France","Copyright":"© Audrey Poree/Alamy","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"The Chauvet Cave preserves the footprints of a prehistoric adolescent who walked barefoot through its passages about 30,000 years ago.","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261017_ChauvetPaintingsFrance\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=International+Archaeology+Day&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261017_0400\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261017_ChauvetPaintingsFrance"},"Ssd":"20261017","Name":"ChauvetPaintingsFrance","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"7438357428","FullDateString":"Oct 17, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Why settle for a planetarium ceiling when Jasper can give you the real thing? That's rather the point of the Jasper Dark Sky Festival, which kicks off today and runs until October 25. The annual event grew from celebrations surrounding Jasper National Park's 2011 designation as a Dark Sky Preserve. The idea is simple: protect natural darkness, then give people plenty of reasons to appreciate it.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.MaligneFest_EN-CA6755477171_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.MaligneFest_EN-CA6755477171_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Under a blanket of stars","Title":"Maligne Lake, Jasper National Park, Alberta","Copyright":"© Andrey Popov/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/54.358091,-117.849547/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-CA&od=2&shading=flat&pp=54.358091,-117.849547;S9;Jasper National Park, Alberta&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261016_MaligneFest\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Jasper+Dark+Sky+Festival&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261016_0400\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261016_MaligneFest"},"Ssd":"20261016","Name":"MaligneFest","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"6755477171","FullDateString":"Oct 16, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"As twilight settles over Wroclaw, golden light spills across rooftops, church towers and one of Central Europe's most striking historic centres. This southwestern Polish city spans islands and waterways linked by more than 100 bridges, blending medieval architecture with vibrant modern life. At its heart is Rynek, a lively Market Square established in the 13th century and home to the Gothic Old Town Hall, one of Wroclaw's most recognisable landmarks.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.WroclawPoland_EN-CA2941585195_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.WroclawPoland_EN-CA2941585195_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Bridges, rooftops and twilight","Title":"View of the Wroclaw Market Square from the Witches' Bridge in Wroclaw, Poland","Copyright":"© Piotr Mitelski/Shutterstock","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/51.10977,17.034634/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-CA&od=2&shading=flat&pp=51.10977,17.034634;S9;Wroclaw, Poland&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261015_WroclawPoland\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Wroclaw&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261015_0400\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261015_WroclawPoland"},"Ssd":"20261015","Name":"WroclawPoland","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"2941585195","FullDateString":"Oct 15, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"The season of big meals, bigger bellies and stocking up for winter is here. In Alaska, brown bears at Lake Clark National Park and Preserve make the most of the food still available in October. They feed on fish, sedges, berries, roots, clams and other foods to build up fat reserves. Some can weigh more than 450 kilograms before entering their dens for hibernation. That stored fat helps them survive the winter, when they do not eat or drink.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.GrizzlySwim_EN-CA2710630781_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.GrizzlySwim_EN-CA2710630781_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Catch, eat, repeat","Title":"Brown bear in Silver Salmon Creek, Lake Clark National Park and Preserve, Alaska, United States","Copyright":"© Danny Green/Nature Picture Library","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/61.147081,-153.734242/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-CA&od=2&shading=flat&pp=61.147081,-153.734242;S9;Lake Clark National Park and Preserve, Alaska, USA&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261014_GrizzlySwim\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Brown+bear&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261014_0400\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261014_GrizzlySwim"},"Ssd":"20261014","Name":"GrizzlySwim","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"2710630781","FullDateString":"Oct 14, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Water seems to be everywhere at Plitvice Lakes National Park in Croatia. Sixteen terraced lakes are linked by a network of waterfalls, streams and cascades that wind through forested limestone canyons. The constantly changing colours of the water, ranging from emerald green to deep blue, are shaped by minerals, sunlight and ever-changing reflections. Established in 1949, Plitvice Lakes is Croatia's oldest and largest national park. The landscape is famous for its tufa barriers, natural limestone formations created as mineral-rich water deposits calcium carbonate over centuries. These barriers continue to grow and change, gradually transforming the park's waterfalls and lakes.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.PlitviceAutumn_EN-CA2443117103_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.PlitviceAutumn_EN-CA2443117103_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"A symphony in blue and green","Title":"Plitvice Lakes National Park, Croatia","Copyright":"© Jan Wlodarczyk/Alamy","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/44.866465,15.581867/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-CA&od=2&shading=flat&pp=44.866465,15.581867;S9;Plitvice Lakes National Park, Croatia&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261013_PlitviceAutumn\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Plitvice+Lakes+National+Park&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261013_0400\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261013_PlitviceAutumn"},"Ssd":"20261013","Name":"PlitviceAutumn","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"2443117103","FullDateString":"Oct 13, 2026"}],"PreloadMediaContents":[{"ImageContent":{"Description":"In Bulgaria's Western Rhodope Mountains, autumn leaves gather beside the rushing waters of Sitovo Waterfall. Near the village of Sitovo, southwest of Plovdiv, the falls tumble beneath an old stone bridge whose arch frames the cascades like a storybook scene. Moss-covered stones and pine trees add shades of green to the autumn landscape, while fallen leaves gather along the water's edge or drift through its pools. The falls become especially lively after rain and during spring snowmelt, when the surrounding woodland echoes with the sound of rushing water.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.SitovoWaterfall_EN-CA2117878012_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.SitovoWaterfall_EN-CA2117878012_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Nature's fall soundtrack","Title":"Autumn waterfalls near Sitovo, Plovdiv Province, Bulgaria","Copyright":"© Nadya85/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/41.926863,24.615841/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-CA&od=2&shading=flat&pp=41.926863,24.615841;S9;Sitovo, Plovdiv Province, Bulgaria&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261026_SitovoWaterfall\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Sitovo+Plovdiv+Bulgaria&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261026_0400\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261026_SitovoWaterfall"},"Ssd":"20261026","Name":"SitovoWaterfall","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"2117878012","FullDateString":"Oct 26, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Some mountains make you work for the view. Mount Sneffels makes you work for the last few hundred metres. Rising to 4,310 metres in Colorado's San Juan Mountains, this fourteener is a familiar sight around Ridgway, Ouray and Telluride. It sits within the 67-square-kilometre Mount Sneffels Wilderness, a protected area designated in 1980. Hikers can reach the mountain from several approaches, including the Yankee Boy Basin and the Blue Lakes area.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.SneffelsAutumn_EN-CA1700205921_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.SneffelsAutumn_EN-CA1700205921_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"'Peak' into Colorado","Title":"Mount Sneffels in the San Juan Mountains near Ridgway, Colorado, United States","Copyright":"© lightphoto/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/38.00354,-107.792695/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-CA&od=2&shading=flat&pp=38.00354,-107.792695;S9;Mount Sneffels, Colorado, United States&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261025_SneffelsAutumn\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Mount+Sneffels&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261025_0400\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261025_SneffelsAutumn"},"Ssd":"20261025","Name":"SneffelsAutumn","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"1700205921","FullDateString":"Oct 25, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Today we're inside the Royal Portuguese Cabinet of Reading in Rio de Janeiro, Brazil, where the humble act of opening a book took on grand architectural ambitions. Founded in 1837 by 43 Portuguese immigrants, just 15 years after Brazil's independence, the institution eventually moved into the building seen here, completed half a century later in a lavish Neo-Manueline style. Shelves soar over 20 metres around a vast reading room, crowned by a monumental stained-glass skylight that makes daylight part of the design.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.PortugueseLibrary_EN-CA0206045106_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.PortugueseLibrary_EN-CA0206045106_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":false},"Headline":"Bookishly extravagant","Title":"Royal Portuguese Cabinet of Reading, Rio de Janeiro, Brazil","Copyright":"© Antonio Salaverry/Shutterstock","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/-22.905431,-43.182116/3?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-CA&od=2&shading=flat&pp=-22.905431,-43.182116;S9;Royal Portuguese Cabinet of Reading, Rio de Janeiro, Brazil&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261024_PortugueseLibrary\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Royal+Portuguese+Cabinet+of+Reading&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261024_0400\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261024_PortugueseLibrary"},"Ssd":"20261024","Name":"PortugueseLibrary","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"0206045106","FullDateString":"Oct 24, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Two grey wolves move through the sagebrush of Yellowstone National Park in Wyoming, home to some of North America's most closely watched wolf packs. Their thick coats help them withstand harsh winters, and their keen senses make them skilled hunters and communicators.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.YellowstoneWolves_EN-CA9692259331_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.YellowstoneWolves_EN-CA9692259331_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Partners in the wild","Title":"Two grey wolves Yellowstone National Park, Wyoming, United States","Copyright":"© John Morrison/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"Grey wolves can communicate through howls, body language, scent marking and a range of vocalisations, including barks, whines and growls.","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261023_YellowstoneWolves\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Wolf+Awareness+Week&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261023_0400\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261023_YellowstoneWolves"},"Ssd":"20261023","Name":"YellowstoneWolves","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"9692259331","FullDateString":"Oct 23, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Few places in South Korea capture the magic of fall quite like Naejangsan National Park, where mountainsides glow in brilliant shades of scarlet, orange, yellow and gold. Located in the country's southwest, the park is particularly famous for its vivid maple colours, making it one of Korea's premier destinations for fall scenery. Its name, meaning 'many secrets in the mountains,' reflects the varied landscapes found throughout the region.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.NaejangsanNP_EN-CA9328142735_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.NaejangsanNP_EN-CA9328142735_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Still waters, vivid colours","Title":"Fall in Naejangsan National Park, South Korea","Copyright":"© Twenty47studio/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/35.481191,126.889374/3?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-CA&od=2&shading=flat&pp=35.481191,126.889374;S9;Naejangsan National Park, South Korea&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261022_NaejangsanNP\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Naejangsan+National+Park&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261022_0400\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261022_NaejangsanNP"},"Ssd":"20261022","Name":"NaejangsanNP","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"9328142735","FullDateString":"Oct 22, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Bridging the gap between old and new, Nguyen Hoang Bridge gives Hue's skyline a fresh connection. Spanning the Perfume River in Vietnam, the modern steel-arch landmark opened to traffic on March 26, 2025. Its design, called 'The Crane Facing Thien Mu,' draws inspiration from a local legend and nearby Thien Mu Pagoda.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.VietnamBridge_EN-CA8865714729_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.VietnamBridge_EN-CA8865714729_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Winging it over the river","Title":"Nguyen Hoang Bridge over the Perfume River, Hue, Vietnam","Copyright":"© VU PHAM VAN/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/16.455292,107.55998/3?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-CA&od=2&shading=flat&pp=16.455292,107.55998;S9;Nguyen Hoang Bridge, Hue, Vietnam&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261021_VietnamBridge\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Hue+Vietnam&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261021_0400\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261021_VietnamBridge"},"Ssd":"20261021","Name":"VietnamBridge","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"8865714729","FullDateString":"Oct 21, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Slow and steady wins the race—and the brown-throated sloth seems perfectly happy to skip the race altogether. On International Sloth Day, this three-toed mammal offers a different les